ok - --write publishes every field atomically with a null failure on a clean run
ok - no_mistakes_run reads the real status shape and refuses a sibling branch's run
ok - fm_nm_select_run chooses the run, and an unusable choice reads as unknown
ok - a hung run head check is bounded, unknown, and sets failure
ok - a worktree off its recorded branch or with an unread branch reads as unknown
ok - a terminal or parked run binds only through the worktree head
ok - only an answered daemon-down suppresses an active run's live claim
ok - a failed no-mistakes read is unknown and sets failure
ok - real fractional transcripts give last turn and used tokens, with remaining unknown
